    {
      "id": "44129770",
      "title": "Handling Form Submission (Reactive Forms)",
      "lectureOrder": 253,
      "videoOrder": 241,
      "sourceHash": "492b4d183f485e7f65ceb2a922cff045933aedcef5e5489f5d7404bcaca0f370",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.48,
          "end": 2.25,
          "en": "So let's start with handling",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.25,
          "end": 4.32,
          "en": "the form submission.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 4.32,
          "end": 7.11,
          "en": "I already got a onSubmit method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 7.11,
          "end": 11.49,
          "en": "but this should now get triggered when the form is submitted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.49,
          "end": 14.67,
          "en": "and handling the submission works just as it does",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.67,
          "end": 17.13,
          "en": "with template driven forms.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.13,
          "end": 20.37,
          "en": "You can listen to the special ngSubmit event",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.37,
          "end": 22.05,
          "en": "that doesn't change,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 22.05,
          "end": 26.7,
          "en": "and you can then call whatever method you want to call here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.7,
          "end": 29.91,
          "en": "What's different compared to the template",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.91,
          "end": 31.47,
          "en": "driven approach though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 31.47,
          "end": 35.37,
          "en": "is that you don't need to pass any argument to onSubmit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 35.37,
          "end": 38.79,
          "en": "because you already have access to the form in your class",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 38.79,
          "end": 43.79,
          "en": "because it was set up and created there after all.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 43.86,
          "end": 47.07,
          "en": "So here in onSubmit, we can simply console log",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 47.07,
          "end": 50.37,
          "en": "this form to look into it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 50.37,
          "end": 52.95,
          "en": "and get an idea of which kind of information",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 52.95,
          "end": 54.543,
          "en": "we can extract from there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 55.74,
          "end": 60.12,
          "en": "So if I save that and then I enter something here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 60.12,
          "end": 63.78,
          "en": "let's say, and I click login,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 63.78,
          "end": 65.97,
          "en": "you see the form group is locked",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 65.97,
          "end": 69.63,
          "en": "and in the end, it's the same kind of form group object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 69.63,
          "end": 72.15,
          "en": "we dealt with before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 72.15,
          "end": 75.39,
          "en": "Because under the hood, Angular manages these forms",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 75.39,
          "end": 78.03,
          "en": "in the same way, it's just the setup work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 78.03,
          "end": 80.43,
          "en": "that differs in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 80.43,
          "end": 84.75,
          "en": "but we still get our pristine property, the status property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 84.75,
          "end": 89.13,
          "en": "the value property, which represents the shape of our form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 89.13,
          "end": 93.53999999999999,
          "en": "and holds the values of our inputs, of our controls.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 93.53999999999999,
          "end": 95.91,
          "en": "We got the controls object, which allows us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 95.91,
          "end": 98.85,
          "en": "to extract more information about the email",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 98.85,
          "end": 102.21000000000001,
          "en": "or password controls, like whether it's pristine",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 102.21000000000001,
          "end": 103.59,
          "en": "or valid and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 103.59,
          "end": 108.513,
          "en": "And that there for all works as before in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 109.62,
          "end": 113.1,
          "en": "But we actually still have a nice extra benefit in our",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 113.1,
          "end": 117.3,
          "en": "TypeScript code compared to the template driven approach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 117.3,
          "end": 120.51,
          "en": "because we got better TypeScript support here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 120.51,
          "end": 124.02,
          "en": "because TypeScript understands the shape of our form now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 124.02,
          "end": 125.4,
          "en": "and therefore, we can now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 125.4,
          "end": 128.73,
          "en": "for example, access controls.email",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 128.73,
          "end": 133.41,
          "en": "because TypeScript knows that we registered a email control.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 133.41,
          "end": 136.5,
          "en": "We can access this.form.value.email",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 136.5,
          "end": 139.47,
          "en": "and that's the kind of TypeScript support we did not get",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 139.47,
          "end": 143.07,
          "en": "before when using template driven forms.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 143.07,
          "end": 146.49,
          "en": "Their value would be of type any",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 146.49,
          "end": 148.07999999999998,
          "en": "because TypeScript wouldn't know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 148.07999999999998,
          "end": 150.12,
          "en": "which kind of controls we have.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 150.12,
          "end": 152.55,
          "en": "But here, getting the entered email",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 152.55,
          "end": 157.55,
          "en": "and the entered password is super easy and type safe",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 157.95,
          "end": 161.913,
          "en": "because we're using this reactive forms approach.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 163.44,
          "end": 165.96,
          "en": "And therefore, of course, I can console.log",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 165.96,
          "end": 170.96,
          "en": "both pieces of information here if I want to, like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 172.53,
          "end": 177.53,
          "en": "With that, again, if we enter our information here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 178.62,
          "end": 182.94,
          "en": "and click login, you see that output here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 182.94,
          "end": 185.52,
          "en": "And that's how we can handle the form submission",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 185.52,
          "end": 187.833,
          "en": "and get hold of the entered values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 188.79,
          "end": 193.79,
          "en": "But what about validation when working with reactive forms?",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
